  "summary": "The third proposal's 'just three copy-paste mistakes' diagnosis is mostly right but overlooks a critical contradiction: the auto-refresh path at tui.py:2636 intentionally calls FeatureFile.list_all() without a board filter (the comment on line 2634 literally reads 'push ALL features for aggregate view'), and the /api/board endpoint in api.go:411-417 aggregates features across all clients — meaning the server-side architecture is designed for unfiltered, cross-board pushes. Blindly replacing all three bare list_all() calls with board-filtered _load_features() would break the webui's aggregate view for multi-board setups. The actual fix needs to distinguish two concerns: (1) the periodic push and auto-mode toggle (tui.py:2093, 2137) should indeed use _load_features(self.active_board) since they're just heartbeats that shouldn't overwrite state with a differently-shaped payload, but (2) the auto-refresh path (tui.py:2636) needs a different solution — either the server should track features per-board-per-client rather than a flat list, or the TUI should send board-tagged features so the server can merge rather than replace. The unconditional assignment at hub.go:354 is the real structural defect: it does a full replace when it should do a merge or at minimum a board-scoped replace. Without fixing the server's replace semantics, any client-side filtering is just choosing which data to lose."
